  "question": {
    "text": "The general value of the real angle $\\theta$, which satisfies the equation. $(\\cos \\theta+i \\sin \\theta)(\\cos 2 \\theta+i \\sin 2 \\theta) \\ldots$$(\\cos n \\theta+t \\sin n \\theta)=1$ is given by, (assuming $k$ is an integer)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2 k \\pi}{n+2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4 k \\pi}{n(n+1)}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4 x \\pi}{n+1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{6 k \\pi}{n(n+1)}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$(\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta)(cos2\\theta+isin2\\theta)...(cosn\\theta+isinn\\theta) = 1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow e^{i\\theta}.e^{i(2\\theta)}.e^{i(3\\theta)}. ...e^{i(n\\theta)} = 1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow e^{i\\theta(1+2+3+...+n}=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow e^{\\frac{in(n+1)\\theta}{2}}=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow cos(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\theta)+isin(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\theta = 1 + 0i$\r\n$\\Rightarrow cos(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\theta)=1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\theta = 2k\\pi$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{4k}{n(n+1)}\\pi$"
  }
}